  rt.1 7-9|kitchen|Asks about spare food then folds the empty grocery bag flat
  rt.2 13-15|porch|Walks a short permitted circuit instead of asking for time alone
  rt.3 20-22|table|Repairs a cardigan button and asks whether Harvey has eaten
  bl.1 losing lottery ticket||A theft from Mrs. Venn's dresser; now a small luck story easier to tell than its origin.
  bl.2 knotted grocery bag||Used repeatedly since leaving the duplex; Gloria dislikes opening it where someone may see it empty.
  bl.3 yellow button||Bought because its color recalled the hospital cup, not because it matched her cardigan.
  bl.4 duplex key|Base.KeyRing|Kept ready for the return home she speaks of as certain.
  bl.5 ridge pebble||Smooth pale stone from the walk she took after Vera's funeral.
  bl.6 folded cleaning notice|Base.Newspaper|Her old handwritten offer wrapped in a newspaper page; an ordinary way to be known again.
  rl.1 Harvey Napier|husband|Married in 1979; he carries practical burdens while she describes their destinations as settled.
  rl.2 Vera Pike|sister, died 1965|Wanted to leave Bardstown; her drowned future is hidden beneath Gloria's harmless outing story.
  rl.3 Bess Pike|mother, died 1981|Prayed through Gloria's hospital stay and was never shown Vera's final letter.
  rl.4 Mrs. Venn|former householder|Trusted Gloria with a dresser key; never noticed a losing lottery ticket was missing.
end

