  bl.1 Frank's cold pipe|Base.Pipe|Not used for tobacco now; holds a rolled bird drawing made by Harvey's mother.
  bl.2 day notebook|Base.Notebook|Started after the outbreak; records distances fairly and his own actions less fairly.
  bl.3 soft pencil|Base.Pencil|Della preferred it to pens for stock sheets; Harvey never returned the last one she lent.
  bl.4 paint-speckled shirt||Green spots belong to Merritt's door repair, which Harvey liked better than car polishing.
  bl.5 bird guide cover||Only the detached cover remains from Celia's guide, carried flat inside the notebook.
  bl.6 kettle lid screw||Kept for the kettle back in Bardstown; Gloria thinks the lid needs replacing rather than another fix.
  rl.1 Gloria Napier|wife|Married in 1979; he respects her ridge walks but describes uncertain routes as workable.
  rl.2 Della Rusk|former coworker|Taught him paint work, lost her job for his theft, then still helped carry Clive in the outbreak.
  rl.3 Clive Penrod|adult neighbor|Injured on the road; Harvey and Della carried him to a farm gate before parting.
  rl.4 Celia Napier|mother, died 1989|Bird watcher whose tiny wren drawing Harvey keeps inside Frank's pipe.
